      "text": "To find the value(s) of \\( x \\) for which \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\), we first need to determine the inverse function \\( f^{-1}(x) \\) of the given function \\( f(x) = 3x - 8 \\).\n\n1. **Find the inverse function \\( f^{-1}(x) \\):**\n\n   Start with the equation \\( y = f(x) = 3x - 8 \\).\n   To find the inverse, we need to solve for \\( x \\) in terms of \\( y \\):\n   \\[\n   y = 3x - 8\n   \\]\n   Add 8 to both sides:\n   \\[\n   y + 8 = 3x\n   \\]\n   Divide both sides by 3:\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{y + 8}{3}\n   \\]\n   Therefore, the inverse function is:\n   \\[\n   f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x + 8}{3}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Set \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\):**\n   We need to find \\( x \\) such that:\n   \\[\n   f(x) = f^{-1}(x)\n   \\]\n   Substitute \\( f(x) = 3x - 8 \\) and \\( f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x + 8}{3} \\):\n   \\[\n   3x - 8 = \\frac{x + 8}{3}\n   \\]\n   To eliminate the fraction, multiply both sides by 3:\n   \\[\n   3(3x - 8) = x + 8\n   \\]\n   Simplify the left side:\n   \\[\n   9x - 24 = x + 8\n   \\]\n   Subtract \\( x \\) from both sides:\n   \\[\n   8x - 24 = 8\n   \\]\n   Add 24 to both sides:\n   \\[\n   8x = 32\n   \\]\n   Divide both sides by 8:\n   \\[\n   x = 4\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( x \\) for which \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\) is \\boxed{4}.",
