      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the value(s) of \\( x \\) for which \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\). We start by determining the inverse function \\( f^{-1}(x) \\) of \\( f(x) = 3x - 8 \\).\n\n### Step 1: Find the inverse function \\( f^{-1}(x) \\)\n\nGiven:\n\\[ f(x) = 3x - 8 \\]\n\nLet \\( y = f(x) \\). Then:\n\\[ y = 3x - 8 \\]\n\nTo find \\( x \\) in terms of \\( y \\), we solve for \\( x \\):\n\\[ y = 3x - 8 \\]\n\\[ y + 8 = 3x \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{y + 8}{3} \\]\n\nThus, the inverse function is:\n\\[ f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x + 8}{3} \\]\n\n### Step 2: Set up the equation \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\)\n\nWe need to find \\( x \\) such that:\n\\[ f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\]\n\nSubstitute \\( f(x) \\) and \\( f^{-1}(x) \\) into the equation:\n\\[ 3x - 8 = \\frac{x + 8}{3} \\]\n\n### Step 3: Solve the equation for \\( x \\)\n\nFirst, eliminate the fraction by multiplying both sides by 3:\n\\[ 3(3x - 8) = x + 8 \\]\n\\[ 9x - 24 = x + 8 \\]\n\nNext, isolate \\( x \\) by subtracting \\( x \\) from both sides:\n\\[ 9x - x - 24 = 8 \\]\n\\[ 8x - 24 = 8 \\]\n\nThen, add 24 to both sides:\n\\[ 8x = 32 \\]\n\nFinally, divide both sides by 8:\n\\[ x = 4 \\]\n\n### Conclusion\n\nThe value of \\( x \\) for which \\( f(x) = f^{-1}(x) \\) is:\n\\[ \\boxed{4} \\]",
